
# 18. AVL Trees

## Question Description
Implement an AVL Tree in C++. An AVL Tree is a self-balancing Binary Search Tree in which the balance factor of every node is -1, 0, or +1. Implement insertion and inorder traversal.

## Test Cases

### Test Case 1
Input: `[10, 20, 30]`

Expected Output (Inorder):
`10 20 30`

### Test Case 2
Input: `[30, 20, 10]`

Expected Output (Inorder):
`10 20 30`

### Test Case 3
Input: `[10, 30, 20]`

Expected Output (Inorder):
`10 20 30`

## Time Complexity
- Insertion: O(log n)
- Search: O(log n)
- Inorder traversal: O(n)

## Space Complexity
- O(n) for storing n nodes.
- O(log n) recursion stack for balanced-tree operations.
